LRdecomposition -- LR decomposition
***********************************

  * Usage: 
        LRdecomposition(A,pivotfunction)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, square and invertible.
      * pivotfunction, a *note function: (Macaulay2Doc)Function,, used for
        pivoting.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, of a list with a permutation
        of the rows of A corresponding to P, and a matrix containing L and R.

Description
===========

Does the PA=LR decomposition on the matrix A, pivoting by the minimal value of
pivotfunction. L can be extracted by the function extractLeftLower, R by
extractRightUpper. This has been implemented with fields of rational functions
in mind.

+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : A=random(QQ^3,QQ^3)                |
|                                        |
|o1 = | 9/2 1/2 3/2 |                    |
|     | 1/2 1   3/4 |                    |
|     | 9/4 3/4 7/4 |                    |
|                                        |
|              3        3                |
|o1 : Matrix QQ  <--- QQ                 |
+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : (perm,LR)=LRdecomposition(A,j->-j);|
+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : perm                               |
|                                        |
|o3 = {0, 1, 2}                          |
|                                        |
|o3 : List                               |
+----------------------------------------+
|i4 : P=transpose (id_(QQ^3))_perm       |
|                                        |
|o4 = | 1 0 0 |                          |
|     | 0 1 0 |                          |
|     | 0 0 1 |                          |
|                                        |
|              3        3                |
|o4 : Matrix QQ  <--- QQ                 |
+----------------------------------------+
|i5 : R=extractRightUpper(LR)            |
|                                        |
|o5 = | 9/2 1/2   3/2   |                |
|     | 0   17/18 7/12  |                |
|     | 0   0     47/68 |                |
|                                        |
|              3        3                |
|o5 : Matrix QQ  <--- QQ                 |
+----------------------------------------+
|i6 : L=extractLeftLower(LR)             |
|                                        |
|o6 = | 1   0    0 |                     |
|     | 1/9 1    0 |                     |
|     | 1/2 9/17 1 |                     |
|                                        |
|              3        3                |
|o6 : Matrix QQ  <--- QQ                 |
+----------------------------------------+
|i7 : L*R==P*A                           |
|                                        |
|o7 = true                               |
+----------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note extractRightUpper: extractRightUpper, -- Extract R from the LR
    decomposition result.
  * *note extractLeftLower: extractLeftLower, -- Extract L from the LR
    decomposition result.

